wg-frag-go is built for the Launchpad PPA with vendored Go dependencies.
Launchpad builders do not provide unrestricted outbound network access, so the
source package must contain the exact dependencies used by the build.

The repository does not track `vendor/`; generate it only while preparing the
source package as shown below.

The PPA targets Ubuntu series while they are in Canonical's standard support
window. The currently configured series are 22.04 (jammy), 24.04 (noble), and
26.04 (resolute). Each series receives its own source build. The version
suffixes are `+jammy1`, `+noble1`, and `+resolute1`; increment the trailing
number when the same release is rebuilt. Launchpad requires a distinct version
for each series, and the GitHub Actions PPA job generates these entries
automatically. EOL series are not backfilled.

Add `ppa:longsleep/golang-backports` as a PPA dependency so the jammy builder
can satisfy `golang-go (>= 2:1.26~)`. The PPA settings page has an "Edit PPA
dependencies" action for this. This is a build-time dependency; users
installing `wg-frag-go` do not need to enable the Go backports PPA.

The binary is statically linked and the package has no series-specific runtime
dependencies. The source package is rebuilt for each target series so that
Launchpad validates the build dependencies in that series. Use a new package
version for every release; Launchpad does not allow reusing a version that was
already published in the PPA.

From a checkout containing the Debian directory, generate the vendored source
package with:

    go mod vendor
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -sa -d
    rm -rf vendor

Upload each generated source changes file with:

    dput ppa:wg-frag/wg-frag-go ../wg-frag-go_<version>_source.changes

The GitHub Actions job performs this upload for all supported series. On a
workflow rerun, `GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT` increments the series suffix (`+jammy1`,
then `+jammy2`, for example).

The GitHub Actions PPA job expects the following values in the `launchpad`
Environment:

* Environment secret `LAUNCHPAD_GPG_PRIVATE_KEY`: ASCII-armored private key
  registered with Launchpad.
* Environment secret `LAUNCHPAD_GPG_PASSPHRASE`: passphrase for that key.
* Environment variable `LAUNCHPAD_GPG_KEY_ID`: full fingerprint or key ID.

The job uses Launchpad's public PPA FTP upload endpoint, so no SSH private key
is required. Keep the PPA environment protected if uploads should require
manual approval.
